      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To gain more insight into the filesystem or network state during those moments of failure, consider adding logging to your Jenkins build and application code. You can also configure Jenkins to capture system and process logs during the build, such as running it as a jailed or headless agent. Additionally, consider using a tool like JMeter or LoadRunner to monitor network activity and file system access during the build run. This will help you visualize and identify any unusual patterns or resource usage that may be contributing to the failure.",
